**Light PLAN** (a line per phase, boundary, ADR; drop unused `intent`, `research_doc`):

```markdown
---
type: plan
task_slug: {slug}
status: planning
created: {YYYY-MM-DD}
spec: "[[SPEC-{slug}]]"
research_doc: "[[RESEARCH-{slug}]]"
intent: <id>
adrs: {M}
summary: "{summary}"
---

## 📝 Implementation Plan
- [ ] {N}. **Phase {N} — {name}** — scope: {files} · exit: `{command}` · risk: {risk} · rollback: {rollback}

## 🚧 Contract Boundaries
### Do not change
- `{path}` — {why}

## 📐 Architecture Decision Records
- ADR-{NNN}: {decision}. **Decided by:** {provenance}
```

Paths are repo-relative; else `Advisory: {intent}` or the sole `none — this task has no contract
boundaries`. `{provenance}`: `user (source: …)` or `agent`. **Light read-back** (after Step 0.1):
(a) the frontmatter carries every key of the template kept; (b) every phase line carries
`scope:`, `exit:`, `risk:` and `rollback:`; (c) `### Do not change` is present and non-empty,
every bullet is one of the three admitted forms, a `none` bullet only as the sole bullet;
(d) `spec_need_verdict` is set. Failures are self-repaired inline. Step 1.5 does not apply:
phases run in order; well over five files is not light: follow the full PLAN text instead and
log that it reads as `full`.
